# Word Document Creation Rules

Rules for consistent, professional Word document generation and formatting.

## 1. Document Structure

- Define heading styles (Heading 1, 2, 3) before generating content.
- Use section breaks (not page breaks) for major document divisions.
- Maintain a minimum of one table of contents field for documents exceeding 5 pages.
- Set default font, font size, and paragraph spacing in the base template.
- Source of truth: PreTeXt XML. DOCX is a derived output, not the authoring format.

## 2. Style Management

- Prefer named styles (Normal, Heading 1, Body Text) over direct formatting.
- When modifying styles, ensure the change propagates consistently through `styles/` configuration.
- Avoid inline formatting for structural elements (use character styles instead).
- Reference: `skills/anthropics/skills/docx` for style manipulation API.

## 3. Templates

- Separate content from presentation by using .dotx templates.
- Store templates in `templates/` with naming convention `templates/<project>-template.dotx`.
- Templates must include: base styles, headers/footers, margins, page numbering.
- Document template usage in the project README.

## 4. Images and Figures

- Embed images at print resolution (300 DPI minimum).
- Use relative paths when linking images in docx for portability.
- Set alt text on all embedded figures for accessibility.
- Prefer vector formats (SVG converted to EMF) for diagrams and charts.
- In PreTeXt: use `<figure>` with `<image>`, `<caption>`, and `<description>`.

## 5. Tables

- Define header row style and repeat header rows across pages.
- Use table styles for consistent border and shading.
- Avoid merged cells in data tables (reserved for layout-only tables).
- Format numbers in tables with consistent decimal precision.
- In PreTeXt: use `<table>` with `<tabular>`, `<row>`, and `<cell>`.

## 6. Cross-References

- Use `<xref>` for internal references in PreTeXt; never hardcode section numbers.
- Use `<cite>` for bibliography references; keep `.bib` file synchronized.
- Run `pretext build` after any reference change to resolve and validate.
